<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><ncx xmlns="http://www.daisy.org/z3986/2005/ncx/" version="2005-1" xml:lang="en"><head><meta name="dtb:uid" content="urn:uuid:4daebda0-fd9b-4195-8c22-de98cbcb3590"/><meta name="dtb:depth" content="2"/><meta name="dtb:totalPageCount" content="0"/><meta name="dtb:maxPageNumber" content="0"/></head><docTitle><text>The money behind the promise</text></docTitle><navMap><navPoint id="nav-1" playOrder="1"><navLabel><text>From the policy to the payment</text></navLabel><content src="text/reader-guide.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-2" playOrder="2"><navLabel><text>Documents, dates and reporting scope</text></navLabel><content src="text/method.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-3" playOrder="3"><navLabel><text>Following the money through to payment</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch001.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-4" playOrder="4"><navLabel><text>Who owes AT&amp;T retirees their pensions?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#chapter-1"/><navPoint id="nav-5" playOrder="5"><navLabel><text>Three dates in the transfer of a pension obligation</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-three-dates-in-the-transfer-of-a-pension-obligation"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-6" playOrder="6"><navLabel><text>The price of a retirement promise</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-price-of-a-retirement-promise"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-7" playOrder="7"><navLabel><text>Following ownership back to Apollo</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-following-ownership-back-to-apollo"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-8" playOrder="8"><navLabel><text>A separate account deserves a closer look</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-a-separate-account-deserves-a-closer-look"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-9" playOrder="9"><navLabel><text>The protection system changes as well</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-protection-system-changes-as-well"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-10" playOrder="10"><navLabel><text>At Prudential, risk moved before the policies</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-at-prudential-risk-moved-before-the-policies"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-11" playOrder="11"><navLabel><text>Reinsurance adds a second contract</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-reinsurance-adds-a-second-contract"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-12" playOrder="12"><navLabel><text>The economic case remains open</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-economic-case-remains-open"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-13" playOrder="13"><navLabel><text>The company that must pay in twenty years</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-company-that-must-pay-in-twenty-years"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-14" playOrder="14"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-15" playOrder="15"><navLabel><text>Why buy the insurer when you already manage its money?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#chapter-2"/><navPoint id="nav-16" playOrder="16"><navLabel><text>The price of the shares and the policyholders’ money</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-the-price-of-the-shares-and-the-policyholders-money"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-17" playOrder="17"><navLabel><text>Apollo buys a more durable relationship and insurance earnings</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-apollo-buys-a-more-durable-relationship-and-insurance-earnings"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-18" playOrder="18"><navLabel><text>KKR buys a larger share of the same earnings</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-kkr-buys-a-larger-share-of-the-same-earnings"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-19" playOrder="19"><navLabel><text>Brookfield separates the owner from the manager</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-brookfield-separates-the-owner-from-the-manager"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-20" playOrder="20"><navLabel><text>A fee moves through the group</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-a-fee-moves-through-the-group"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-21" playOrder="21"><navLabel><text>Blackstone puts a value on a secure contract</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-blackstone-puts-a-value-on-a-secure-contract"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-22" playOrder="22"><navLabel><text>Duration has a value, and so does risk</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-duration-has-a-value-and-so-does-risk"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-23" playOrder="23"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch003.xhtml#c2-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-24" playOrder="24"><navLabel><text>The Bermuda balance sheet behind an American annuity</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#chapter-3"/><navPoint id="nav-25" playOrder="25"><navLabel><text>Two contracts behind each benefit payment</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-two-contracts-behind-each-benefit-payment"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-26" playOrder="26"><navLabel><text>Keeping the securities, passing on the return</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-keeping-the-securities-passing-on-the-return"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-27" playOrder="27"><navLabel><text>Apollo invests within an agreed mandate</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-apollo-invests-within-an-agreed-mandate"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-28" playOrder="28"><navLabel><text>Each form of collateral has its own conditions</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-each-form-of-collateral-has-its-own-conditions"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-29" playOrder="29"><navLabel><text>The treaty allows several stages of intervention</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch004.xhtml#c3-the-treaty-allows-several-stages-of-intervention"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-30" playOrder="30"><navLabel><text>Bermuda brings together several forms of reinsurance</text></navLabe