e-map"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-41" playOrder="41"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch005.xhtml#c4-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-42" playOrder="42"><navLabel><text>Who gets the investment returns?</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#chapter-5"/><navPoint id="nav-43" playOrder="43"><navLabel><text>Bringing two rates onto comparable terms</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-bringing-two-rates-onto-comparable-terms"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-44" playOrder="44"><navLabel><text>Access to the money has a price</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-access-to-the-money-has-a-price"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-45" playOrder="45"><navLabel><text>The commission begins with a sale</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-the-commission-begins-with-a-sale"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-46" playOrder="46"><navLabel><text>At Athene, more assets and a narrower margin</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-at-athene-more-assets-and-a-narrower-margin"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-47" playOrder="47"><navLabel><text>Management fees come before the insurer’s earnings</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-management-fees-come-before-the-insurers-earnings"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-48" playOrder="48"><navLabel><text>KKR sets out the revenues connected to its insurer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-kkr-sets-out-the-revenues-connected-to-its-insurer"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-49" playOrder="49"><navLabel><text>An additional return can pay for useful work</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-an-additional-return-can-pay-for-useful-work"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-50" playOrder="50"><navLabel><text>From contract growth to group earnings</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-from-contract-growth-to-group-earnings"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-51" playOrder="51"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch006.xhtml#c5-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-52" playOrder="52"><navLabel><text>The regulatory price of a promise</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#chapter-6"/><navPoint id="nav-53" playOrder="53"><navLabel><text>An investment becomes a claim on a reinsurer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-an-investment-becomes-a-claim-on-a-reinsurer"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-54" playOrder="54"><navLabel><text>Protection begins in the contract</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-protection-begins-in-the-contract"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-55" playOrder="55"><navLabel><text>The rating meets the structure</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-the-rating-meets-the-structure"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-56" playOrder="56"><navLabel><text>In Bermuda, follow the payments through time</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-in-bermuda-follow-the-payments-through-time"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-57" playOrder="57"><navLabel><text>Nine valuations, and the comparisons still to build</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-nine-valuations-and-the-comparisons-still-to-build"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-58" playOrder="58"><navLabel><text>Capital savings can support a real service</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-capital-savings-can-support-a-real-service"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-59" playOrder="59"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch007.xhtml#c6-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-60" playOrder="60"><navLabel><text>When risks return to the insurer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#chapter-7"/><navPoint id="nav-61" playOrder="61"><navLabel><text>One crisis, two branches of the calculation</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-one-crisis-two-branches-of-the-calculation"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-62" playOrder="62"><navLabel><text>The capital requirement rises with the risks</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-the-capital-requirement-rises-with-the-risks"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-63" playOrder="63"><navLabel><text>Rights over the assets follow their own timetable</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-rights-over-the-assets-follow-their-own-timetable"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-64" playOrder="64"><navLabel><text>Cash needs run through the scenario</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-cash-needs-run-through-the-scenario"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-65" playOrder="65"><navLabel><text>The cost of restoring credit quality</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-the-cost-of-restoring-credit-quality"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-66" playOrder="66"><navLabel><text>Resilience depends on the portfolio that comes back</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-resilience-depends-on-the-portfolio-that-comes-back"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-67" playOrder="67"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch008.xhtml#c7-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-68" playOrder="68"><navLabel><text>The strength of an insurer’s promise</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#chapter-8"/><navPoint id="nav-69" playOrder="69"><navLabel><text>The obligation belongs to a named insurer</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-the-obligation-belongs-to-a-named-insurer"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-70" playOrder="70"><navLabel><text>A group can support the insurer and earn revenue from it</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-a-group-can-support-the-insurer-and-earn-revenue-from-it"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-71" playOrder="71"><navLabel><text>Time can provide an economic advantage</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-time-can-provide-an-economic-advantage"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-72" playOrder="72"><navLabel><text>Stress tests illuminate part of the journey</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-stress-tests-illuminate-part-of-the-journey"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-73" playOrder="73"><navLabel><text>In France, the investment option defines the guarantee</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-in-france-the-investment-option-defines-the-guarantee"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-74" playOrder="74"><navLabel><text>An annuity changes the relationship with capital</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-an-annuity-changes-the-relationship-with-capital"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-75" playOrder="75"><navLabel><text>Protection after failure has its own boundaries</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-protection-after-failure-has-its-own-boundaries"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-76" playOrder="76"><navLabel><text>Following the policy’s payment chain</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-following-the-policys-payment-chain"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-77" playOrder="77"><navLabel><text>Further reading</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-further-reading"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-78" playOrder="78"><navLabel><text>Sources</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch009.xhtml#c8-sources"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-79" playOrder="79"><navLabel><text>The promise has to reach its recipient</text></navLabel><content src="text/conclusion.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-80" playOrder="80"><navLabel><text>Twenty-one terms for following the promise</text></navLabel><content src="text/glossary.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-81" playOrder="81"><navLabel><text>The records behind the opening and conclusion</text></navLabel><content src="text/synthesis-sources.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-82" playOrder="82"><navLabel><text>List of infographics</text></navLabel><content src="text/figures.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-83" playOrder="83"><navLabel><text>Edition and rights</text></navLabel><content src="text/colophon.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-84" playOrder="84"><navLabe